# WCAG Accessibility

The CU mode is a **mobile-first, public-facing application** used by visitors at a stadium, including users with disabilities and assistive tech. All CU UI (and any text Kit projects to the frontend) must follow WCAG 2.1/2.2 AA. This includes new features.

> **If a proposed design conflicts with WCAG**, do NOT silently work around it. Surface the conflict to the user explicitly so they can talk it through with the designer. State which WCAG criterion is at risk, what the violation is, and what alternatives exist.

> **Do not add visible copy that is not in the design** for accessibility alone. Use existing labels/placeholders, ARIA, and `.sr-only` helper text when a programmatic hint helps screen readers. If visible instructions or error copy are needed, escalate to design — do not invent new on-screen sentences in code.

Examples of conflicts worth escalating: contrast ratios under 4.5:1 for body text, touch targets under 44×44 px, keyboard-inaccessible custom widgets, animations without a reduced-motion fallback, color-only state indication, untranslatable hardcoded strings.

## Scope

- **Always applies**: `web-viewer-sample-main/src/features/cu/**` and any `streaming/overlays/**` rendered in CU mode.
- **Also applies**: text projected from Kit (`interactions.json` `ui.title`, `npcConfig.greeting`, etc.) — Kit text becomes part of the CU UI.
- **Doesn't apply**: `features/dev/**` (developer tools, intentionally English-only and not user-facing).

## Checklist for new CU features

Run through this **before** writing the code, not after:

1. **Semantic HTML first** — `<button>`, `<a>`, `<nav>`, `<main>`, `<dialog>` etc. before custom `<div role="...">`.
2. **Localize every string** from day 1 via `t('namespace.key')`. Add the key to `en/sv/fr/es.json` simultaneously. Kit-projected text uses i18n key references in `interactions.json` (e.g. `"interactions.<id>.greeting"`) — see `localization.mdc`.
3. **Keyboard reachable** — every interactive element via Tab; arrow keys for listbox/tablist/carousel; `Escape` closes modals and panels.
4. **Focus visible** — never `outline: none` without a `:focus-visible` replacement. Project default in `src/app/index.css` already handles this.
5. **ARIA where needed** — `aria-label` for icon-only buttons, `aria-pressed` for toggles, `aria-expanded`/`aria-controls` for disclosures, `aria-modal="true"` for modals, `aria-live="polite"` for status regions, `role="tabpanel"`/`role="tablist"` for tabbed UIs.
6. **Touch target ≥ 44×44 px** (WCAG 2.5.5 AAA, but our minimum). For tiny visual elements use `border: <n>px solid transparent` + negative margin to expand the hit area without changing layout — see `OnboardingOverlay.css` `.onboarding-dot`.
7. **Don't rely on color alone** — pair color with icon, label, or pattern. **Checklist 1.4.1 = Yes** (May 2026 audit): CU controls use non-color cues (`aria-pressed`, switch glyphs, icons + text on chips, active borders) — re-verify when adding new toggle-only or icon-only controls.
8. **Respect `prefers-reduced-motion`** — `index.css` already disables long animations globally; new bespoke animations should also honour it.
9. **TTS for any read-aloud content** — see `text-to-speech.mdc`. Voice language must match text language.
10. **Restore focus** when closing modals/overlays (capture `document.activeElement` on mount, restore on unmount).
11. **Skip-to-content** — already provided by `StreamOnlyWindow.tsx` `.skip-to-content` link + `<main id="main-content">`. Don't break it.

